+// A tab the host has never shown has no size: its view gets one from the
+// host's first attachment (attachment_lease.cc), and until then its page is
+// laid out in a viewport of 0 x 0 and its compositor draws nothing. A capture
+// of it never has a first frame, the renderer's video source gives up after
+// ten seconds (VideoCaptureImpl::kCaptureStartTimeout) and the page's
+// getDisplayMedia() fails: the share "starts and stops". Chrome sizes a tab
+// when it is made (the size of the tab it is opened from); the bridge gives a
+// tab that is shared before it was ever shown the size of the tab that asks.
+// The host's attachment sets the view's frame again when it shows the tab.
+// The page's visibility does not change here: see
+// ReArcTabDelegate::KeepsPageHiddenWhileCaptured.
+void GiveSizeToUnshownTab(content::WebContents* target,
+                          content::WebContents* asker) {
+  if (!target->GetSize().IsEmpty()) {
+    return;
+  }
+  const gfx::Size size = asker->GetSize();
+  if (!size.IsEmpty()) {
+    target->Resize(gfx::Rect(size));
+  }
+}
